<title>COLOMBIA: Colombian stocks end firmer.</title>
<headline>Colombian stocks end firmer.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombian share price indexes rose, led by banks, cement and brewing, in heavy trade ahead of the two-day Christmas break.</p>
<p>Bogota's IBB index edged up 0.08 percent to 842.05 amid a 2 billion peso volume while Medellin's IBOMED general price index gained 0.39 percent closing the session at 13,319.51 amid a higher-than-average 22 billion peso volume.</p>
</text>
